00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.020 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Lara Croft at the beginning of this game  is someone who is searching for answers  and in almost a level of being obsessed  with finding these answers you're seeing  a level of determination and almost  stubbornness in a way to follow leads  that could put her life on the line so  it's this extra determination this  willingness to go further to do things  that other humans maybe wouldn't be  willing to do that makes her especially  unique in this game we had a fantastic  opportunity for the reboot to redesign  Lara from the ground up and in a lot of  ways that's very daunting also very  exciting for our team kam was a big part  of that he talks very passionately about  what it takes to construct Lara Croft  but a lot of that comes down to what  know is looking for and what I'm looking  for as far as who she is and and why one  of the exciting things about bringing  Lara to life this time is we're able to  leverage new technology to do that but  before I get into that it's important to  start with Lara's characterization what  was important for us in the reboot and  even more so going forward even as we  take lara farther down her journey as a  as a character was to maintain that  sense of humanity that sense of  relatability that this isn't a superhero  this is someone like URI whose thrust  into these extraordinary situations and  rises to the occasion so it's not that  she doesn't feel fear it's that she is  able to muster courage to overcome that  fear she's always been academic and  smart and strong in her own way but she  has this new confidence and this drive  to try to discover these truths it's  unlocked and kindled a fire inside of  her wanting to find out what these these  ancient secrets could actually mean and  and her father's passion something that  she didn't understand before she's  starting to grapple with and understand  this is not only something that she's  interested in but as part of a family  legacy and in ways you could say it's  reckless but it's really a story about  her becoming who she's meant to be being  a Tomb Raider is something that not  anyone can do you know Lara is uniquely  qualified to be who she's meant to be  which is the Tomb Raider we really  wanted in this game to put Lara into  this world and make her look as if she  really existed in that environment so as  she goes through her adventure she'll  get dirty she'll get bloody if she gets  attacked she'll also get snow on her  snow accumulate on her shoulders if  she's in a snowy environment we're  really trying to push that physicality  in order to really ground Lara in this  environment and make her look like she's  a part of this world as you're running  through the world you see that  nervousness on her face when you're in a  scary tomb or she's seen a trap and she  knows there may be a trap around any  corner that we place Lara in that moment  or whether she's affected by if she's  scrambling around in the dirt she's  gonna get dirty and if she's going  through water she's gonna get wet and if  she's dammit she's gonna get bloody and  all of these facets of both capturing  her emotions but really translating  those in a way where even as you're  playing the game she feels alive in that  same way when Brandon Fernandez our  animation director imagines Lara Croft  in this world he sees her as an active  partner in whatever is happening so if  she's in a tight claustrophobic space  she will touch the walls and be aware of  her her surroundings if if she takes a  particularly hard fall you'll see her  clutch her side or her head  to acknowledge the damage if if you see  lhara you know in a particularly damaged  state she'll start to be woozy and  stammered around in the world there's a  scene in the last game where she got hit  in the face by Vlad with a gun this is  in that scene where she first kill scene  where it was transformational for her so  I wanted to take some of that game and  some of that history and put it into  this game for that sense of continuity  so if you look really carefully at her  model you'll see that a little left over  scar from that from that scene we wanted  her to react to the environment not only  in the sense that when she's cold and  she'll she'll rub herself or when she  walks by a fire she'll warm her hands so  she's actually a part of this world  she's actually exists in there and it  makes people believe that this is a real  person  one of the most challenging things about  this version of Lara we started using  facial blend shapes in this game which  we never had in the last game but by  incorporating this technology we are  actually able to capture a lot of the  nuances in the actors performance Lara  has over a hundred facial blend shapes  that she uses in order to to show her  emotions in order to talk and blink and  what it allows us to do is really  capture that the every nuance and  Camila's performance and show it in game  and it's it's quite stunning when you  look at it but the hard part really is  just a balance all of that all of the  shapes so they look correct and as she  stays on character that's always been a  really big challenge to make her to look  like a believable character and that  she's she has human emotions and if we  can convey that in the blend shapes I  think that was that was one of the  biggest challenges we've taken the hair  technology from the last game and we  built on that and made a very robust  system a much more powerful system than  we had in the last game her hair  actually now has up to 30,000 strands we  put a lot of work into the physics as  well so when the wind blows it the  ponytail will blow very naturally when  she turns a head the ponytail will roll  off her shoulders and that hair is so  important to to us to get right because  it's such an iconic part of her  character we put a lot of work into  making it look just perfect in some way  she represents adventure that she  embodies everything that's awesome and  exciting about action-adventure games so  whether it's solving puzzles or  platforming or combat or exploration or  great rewards and great storytelling  that all  this is really embodied by Lara Croft  and it's it's a pleasure to be able to  take something that's so unique and  singular but apply it to an experience  that's so universal and exciting

